# Frozen candidate, not executed

This is a separate public controlled scene. The original default-view attempt1 and its failure are untouched. No algorithm, model, threshold, core protocol or Source03 file changes.

The evaluator reads only the actual own camera position and rotation to choose placement. MuJoCo cameras look along local -Z; the normalized XY projection of `-cam_xmat[:,2]` sets the actual forward direction. The candidate checks orthonormality and nearly horizontal orientation, then places original red_infantry body center 2.3m forward. The fixed compiled world-axis X/Y slides and actual resulting position are checked. Front armor +X normal faces the camera. Front plate is .31m in front of body center, so its horizontal camera distance is 1.99m. Original role_v23 armor, calibration, K/D and detect_color=0 stay unchanged. No occlusion/detection success is assumed.

Only evaluator `SCENE.json` receives placement positions. Neither peer nor `build_observation` receives scene metadata, opponent position, target labels or an ideal angle. Own captured sensors and actual RGB remain the only algorithm input. Scene setup is before the one neutral actual 2ms physics step and exposure; timestamps are never edited.

Peer instrumentation records at most 64 scalar local phases in memory: original complete JSONL line, original strict raw decode, actual engine compute, bridge begin and DDS publish. It runs exactly the original bound functions, returns exactly their result, writes nothing to protocol stdout, and persists phases once after inner close. It does not add a callback spinner, extra image or postdeadline wait. Only this artifact peer catches SIGTERM/SIGINT by raising SystemExit, triggering the existing resource finally; repeated TERM cannot interrupt cleanup, while the original outer SIGKILL remains authoritative. The original engine.close budget is still 1s. Observer drain and final evidence writer use only the remaining diagnostic tail bounded to 1.10s from cancellation/finally entry, within original outer1.3/host1.5. Diagnostic disk writing uses one daemon writer with at most a 30ms remaining-budget join; blocked or failed writes are unknown/incomplete and cannot hold the resource closer. Callback summary is embedded in PEER_PHASES.json, not a separate SUMMARY file. Abrupt kill or a delayed Python signal callback can still lose this in-memory evidence; missing or partial phases then remain unknown. `line_wait_begin` includes all time waiting for a fresh request, including prior camera setup, so it is **not transport duration**. Linux local timestamps are not subtracted from HostQPC. Separate observer callbacks retain exact source-context/stamp, with the same bounded read-only journal as first-frame01.

The handler is installed inside the protected try and reinstalled after actual rclpy initialization, before any reset/image. Its first-cancellation timestamp is latched once; repeated signals return without refreshing that timestamp or the evidence deadline. SIGKILL remains uncatchable. Signal handling during a long native extension call is not claimed to be prompt; external owned-tree cleanup remains the proof.

Root alone executes after the resource freeze ends. Commands, under the already checked Humble environment on Linux and from repo root on Windows:

```text
/root/polar-humble-ext4-20261014-01/venv/bin/python /mnt/c/Users/lulu/Desktop/claude/polarsimulation/polar-rm-simulator/artifacts/pb2025-aim-controlled-probe-20261014-01/register_linux.py --label attempt1 --robot-id blue_hero
.venv-sim/Scripts/python.exe artifacts/pb2025-aim-controlled-probe-20261014-01/probe_host.py --label attempt1 --manifest artifacts/pb2025-aim-controlled-probe-20261014-01/registered_attempt1/AIM_PLUGINS.json
```

Fresh preparation/reset precedes real capture. Only one original exposure is sent, with original capture+.08 and control .15 gates. It is never resent or retimed; returned action is never applied. Original reset2s/graph1s stay unchanged. All capture evidence writes happen after strict act/failure. This probe is resource-only, not SDK/live qualification. The original scene's manually inspected empty wall/sky view is not mixed with this candidate's future results.
